(850, 'Jayanth Baligari', 'baligarijayanthkumar331@gmail.com', '9908264672', 'Subject: Application for Graduate Engineer Trainee - Production/Quality- B.Jayanthkumar with 9 years of experience in QA -Dept as Sr. Engineer in Mechanical Commodity ( Automotive, Sheet metals fabrication industry) Interested to learn SMS, CCM or Mechani', 'Dear Sir,\r\nGood Evening,\r\nGreetings for the day.\r\n\r\n\r\nMy name is Jayanth kumar,I am writing to express my strong interest in the \"Graduate Engineer Trainee \"position within your Production/Quality departments. While I bring over 9 years of robust experience in Quality Assurance Dept as a Senior Engineer, I am eager to\" pivot my career into the Steel manufacturing sector\", an industry I have long admired for its scale and technical complexity.Although my previous 9 years were outside of steel manufacturing, I have mastered & Certified Quality Management Systems (QMS ISO9001:2015 IA), Root Cause Analysis (RCA), and process optimization with APQP , PPAP & NDT level 2 requirements as well as my Audit Skill in vendor management & inhouse System. I can immediately apply these \"Quality First\" principles to your production lines.I am well-versed in industry standards and have a proven track record of reducing defects and improving through put skills that are universal to any manufacturing floor.\r\n\r\n\r\nSir, I have attached my resume for your review and would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my background in QA and my passion for mechanical engineering can benefit your plant.\r\n\r\nKindly please provide a small opportunity as an Trainee to restart my carrier in steel industry.\r\n\r\n\" Immediate Joiner\"\r\n\r\n\r\nThank you for your time and consideration.\r\n\r\n\r\nThanks & Regards\r\nB.Jayanthkumar,', '2026-03-31 13:18:42'),
