(860, 'Ashok Kumar Pattanaik', 'pattanaik.ashok@gmail.com', '08889125551', 'carrier opportunity ', 'ASHOK KUMAR PATTANAIK\r\nEmail:akpattanaik2004@yahoo.co.in/ akpattanaik@rediffmail.com/ pattanaik.ashok@gmail.com\r\nPhone: +91 8889125551/ 7999509869\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDear Hiring Manager,\r\nI am writing to express my strong interest in exploring senior leadership opportunities within your esteemed organization. With over 30 years of rich and diversified experience across Human Resource Management, Industrial Relations (IR), and Corporate Affairs, I bring a legacy of driving people-centric strategies, regulatory compliance, and workforce harmony across the steel, cement, and heavy manufacturing sectors.\r\nCurrently, I serve as the  Vice President â€“ HRM at Aarti Steels Ltd., where I lead multi-location IR strategies, Long-Term Settlements (LTS), and end-to-end statutory compliance. My proactive engagement approach has consistently fostered strong relationships with labor unions, reduced industrial disruptions, and ensured seamless alignment with evolving labor laws.\r\nMy career journey has been shaped by pivotal roles at leading conglomerates like Ultratech Cement (Aditya Birla Group), Grasim Industries, and the MSP Group, where I successfully:\r\nâ€¢	Negotiated complex union matters leading to a drastic reduction in work stoppages and zero man-days lost during critical project phases.\r\nâ€¢	Rolled out HRIS tools like PeopleSoft to enhance process transparency, data accuracy & operational efficiency.\r\nâ€¢	Spearheaded workforce rationalization and large-scale restructuring through VRS/PMR with zero productivity impact.\r\nâ€¢	Ensured 100% compliance during labor audits and industrial inspections, often setting benchmarks in IR governance and labor law adherence.\r\nMy role extends beyond IR into corporate governance, crisis management, stakeholder liaison, and strategic HR policy development. From managing plant-level administration to overseeing community relations and project clearances for greenfield and brownfield expansions, I have consistently contributed to business continuity, operational safety, and social license to operate.\r\nWhat sets me apart is my ability to balance business imperatives with empathetic workforce engagement, having earned accolades like the CII Best IR Practices Award. I believe in building resilient teams, fostering a culture of trust, and aligning people strategies with organizational goals to unlock long-term value.\r\nI am now seeking to channel my experience and leadership into a forward-looking organization that values operational excellence, ethical HR practices, and sustainable growth. I am confident that my proven track record in industrial relations, legal risk management, and strategic HR leadership makes me a strong asset for your leadership team.\r\nI welcome the opportunity to discuss how I can contribute to your organizational vision and would be honored to further elaborate on my experiences in a personal interaction. Thank you for considering my application.\r\nSincerely,\r\nAshok Kumar Pattanaik\r\n', '2026-04-02 11:03:43'),
