(1110, 'MANMOHAN   GUPTA', 'man220668@gmail.com', '09833069404', 'Suitable position ', 'MANMOHAN GUPTA FCA\r\nRosa-402, Crystal Palace, Plot-890-894, Sector-20, Belapur Gaon - 400614  \r\nMobile – 9833069404\r\nE-mail:- man220668@gmail.com and gupta2206@rediffmail.com \r\nSummary:  	A Chartered Accountant with 32+ years of experience in Corporate Laws, Accounts, Finance, Audit, Investment related issue and Taxation matters, RTA of MF activities and back-office operations.\r\nAbility to build, lead & motivate teams with good interpersonal relationships.\r\nAnalytical skills combined with organized and focused approach. Ability to visualize opportunities and zeal take up challenges. \r\nExperiences:  \r\n\r\nOct 22 till date      Working as SVP & CFO after joining MD & CEO  \r\n\r\nAug 2021 to Sept 2022        In-Charge CEO in UTIITSL Navi Mumbai. Responsibilities include overall charge of all operational, marketing, administrative and accounts finance functions of the Company having network of 4 regional offices and 47 branches across India.   \r\n\r\nApril 2016 to Aug 2021	Senior Vice President (Corporate Accounts) in UTI Infrastructure Technology & Services Limited (UTIITSL), Navi Mumbai. \r\n                                                Responsibilities include overall in-charge of accounting, finance, reconciliation, and taxation related matters. Preparation of various types of MIS for Board and its committees. Looking into various Audits. Implementation of advice/recommendation of Audits and IFC Consultants reports. In – Charge of PAN processing activities, Secretarial and Legal department w.e.f. Jan 2020. Also designated as Appellate authorities under RTI Act w.e.f. In-Charge of Rajbhasha Vibhag since 2016. Also looking after HR related activities in absence of HR-Head. Also Taking care of day to day’s activities of Company in case leave/absence of MD & CEO. Reporting to MD & CEO.     \r\n\r\nMarch 2009 to March 2016 	Vice President (Corporate Accounts) in UTI Infrastructure Technology and Services Limited (formerly known as UTI Technology Services Ltd), Navi Mumbai. Responsibilities: Finalization of Corporate  centralized accounts having more than 80 branches, Financial analysis of books of accounts, Handling Income tax, Service tax and LBT related matters, working capital management, management of receivable and payable, Investment of surplus funds Internal & Operational Audit, Cost control, Cost reduction, Internal Control, Preparation of capital and revenue budget, Liaison with banks, Staff training and Preparation of quarterly accounts and segmental analysis and other financial MIS. Reporting to MD & CEO. \r\n                                                Designated as Chief Financial officer w e f 28.05.2014.\r\n\r\nDec. 2004 to Feb. 2009: 	Assistant Vice President (Corporate Accounts) in UTI Technology Services Limited, Navi Mumbai \r\nResponsibilities: Reconciliation & Accounting work supervision, ensuring day to day passing of vouchers, cash flow analysis, taxation matters, working capital management, Filing of Income tax, TDS and Service tax returns, Financial Budget preparation, Finalization of books of accounts, Liaison with banks and Preparation of financial MIS. Reporting to Chief Executive Officer. \r\n\r\nJan. 2002 to Nov. 2004:	Branch Manager, Kolkata Main Branch of UTI Technology Services Ltd (formerly Known as Unit Trust of India Investor Services Ltd).\r\nResponsibilities: Processing of UTI MF sales applications, monitoring ‘post sale services’ of UTI MF schemes, issue of Statement of accounts, redressing the complaints of investors and distributors, reconciliation of MF schemes bank accounts & unit capital, dealing with Internal Auditors, Preparation of various MIS etc. Reporting to Vice President-Corporate Operations.\r\n \r\nDec. 1999 to Dec. 2001:	Regional Manager (Eastern India) of UTIISL. \r\n                                                Responsibilities: Overseeing the functioning of all branch offices of eastern India. Taking case of all Operational and administrative activities viz processing of schemes sales application, issue of unit certificates, Statement of accounts, redressing the grievances of investors, distributors & franchisee offices. Reconciliation of schemes units’ capital and Income distributions. HR and other miscellaneous activities of regional office, Internal & Operational Audit, Staff training and Preparation of various MIS. Reporting to CEO. \r\n\r\nApr. 1996 to Nov. 1999: 	Asst Manager from Apr 1996 to Jun 1999 and Manager from July 1999 to Nov. 1999 of Unit Trust of India Investor Services Ltd (UTIISL). Responsibilities: Reconciliation of unit capital & dividend warrants accounts. Administrative and personnel activities relating to Kolkata branch office. Reporting to Regional Manager-Eastern India.						\r\n\r\nAug. 1994 to Mar 1996: 	M/s S. R. Batliboi & Co. (A member of Ernst & Young international) Kolkata from August 1994 to March 1996. Responsibilities include Audit & Certification of financial statements of corporate sectors, Various Banks, Educational & Charitable Institutions.\r\n\r\nEducation:\r\n•	Chartered Accountancy 		May’ 94, Becoming FCA Sept.’99.\r\n•	Company Secretary (Intermediate) 	55%	June’1994.\r\n•	B.Com. Calcutta University 	64%		1989  \r\n•	Certificate in Information Technology from CMC Ltd 1999.\r\n                    \r\nProfessional Upgradation:\r\n•	“Understanding Financial Market, Institutions & Instruments” conducted by ‘Indian Institute of Capital Market, Navi-Mumbai during June’98.\r\n•	“Personality Development, Effective Communication, Managerial Skill conducted by ‘Xavier Institute of Management, Mumbai’ in May 2000.\r\n•	Secured 85% marks in “Process knowledge evolution” examination on Operational activities of UTI Mutual Fund in Nov.’2001.\r\n•	Internal Audit training programme on ISO 9001:2000 Quality Management System & Audit Management conducted by ICS Technologies in Sept 2005.\r\n•	2 days programme on Audit Committee by Indian institute of Corporate affairs in March 2024.\r\n•	3 days management development programme by Indian Institute of Management Indore in Jan 2024.  \r\n \r\n•	KYC and PMLA workshop conducted by FICCI. Risk Management by DnB. Training on incidence of Income Tax on Employee. \r\n\r\n•	Regularly attending Seminars and lectures based on Companies Act, 2013 and allied Laws, GST Act 2017 and Income Tax Act, 1961 organised by ICAI.\r\n\r\n•	Attended RTI workshop by NHRAD in June 2108 and Nov 2025 \r\n\r\n•	Member of Bombay Chartered Accountants Society and Navi Mumbai branch of WIRC of ICAI.     \r\n\r\nOther Achievements\r\nRecognition of Excellence for exceptional calibre and contribution to the world of finance in category of “Corporate governance and compliance” for three consecutive years in CFO100 for FY22, FY23 and FY24.\r\n\r\nPersonal Details:\r\nFathers’ Name: Late Shri. Kailash Nath Gupta\r\nDate of Birth: 22nd June’ 1968.\r\nMarital Status: Married.\r\nInterests: Book Reading, Postage Stamp collection, Traveling, Listening classical music and Gazals.\r\n\r\nPresent Address: \r\n“Rosa” Wing, flat – 402, Crystal Palace,\r\nPlot no. 890-894 & 962-963, Sector-20, Belapur Gaon,\r\nNear Belapur Lake, Navi Mumbai – 400 614.\r\n\r\nLanguages Known: \r\nHindi, Brijbhasha, English and Bengali,    \r\n\r\nIT Knowledge:\r\nWorking knowledge of MS office, Tally ERP 9 Prime.  \r\n\r\nNative Address:\r\nD-904, Panchsheel Apartments, 493/B/1, G T Road (South),\r\nShibpore, Howrah – 711102, (WB). \r\n  \r\nReferences \r\n1.	Dr. Gulshan Rai, former National Cybersecurity Chief and Independent Director of UTI Infrastructure Technology And Services Limited. Mobile -9810643244 and 7011417540.\r\n\r\n2.	Sri. M. Parameswaran, Ex- Chief Executive Officer, UTI Infrastructure Technology And Services Limited. Mobile – 9820046503.  \r\n\r\n3.	Sri Ramgopal Sharma FCA, Partner – Sharma Shah Associates, Mumbai. Mobile - 9619765107   \r\n  \r\n\r\n\r\nManmohan Gupta\r\n', '2026-06-08 14:52:09'),
