(1129, 'Surya Veena Adarsh Niketan Trust', 'rashmiranjan@svantindia.org.in', '07034777277', 'Request for CSR Partnership and Financial Support for Project UDDAN – Empowering India\'s Youth through Education, Innovation & Employability', 'Greetings from Surya Veena Adarsh Niketan Trust!!\r\nWe are pleased to present Project UDDAN(U.P & Delhi Govt.Recommended ), a transformative initiative designed to empower students, teachers, and young professionals through skill development, entrepreneurship, innovation, career guidance, psychometric assessment, women empowerment, and capacity building in alignment with the vision of the National Education Policy (NEP) 2020.\r\nEstablished in 2010, Surya Veena Adarsh Niketan Trust has been working tirelessly in the fields of education, skill development, women empowerment, and social transformation. Over the years, we have collaborated with schools, colleges, universities, government institutions, and corporate organizations, positively impacting thousands of learners and educators across India.\r\nIndia is home to the world\'s largest youth population, yet millions of young people continue to face challenges related to employability, career awareness, entrepreneurial exposure, technological skills, and access to quality mentoring. Project UDDAN has been conceptualized to bridge these gaps by providing structured interventions that prepare students for the rapidly evolving future of work.\r\nThrough this project, we aim to:\r\n• Promote entrepreneurship, startup culture, and innovation among youth.\r\n• Provide AI & Robotics training to build future-ready skills.\r\n• Conduct psychometric and career assessments to help students make informed career decisions.\r\n• Empower girl students through training, counselling, and financial independence programs.\r\n• Enhance teacher effectiveness through NEP 2020-oriented professional development.\r\n• Foster critical thinking, creativity, leadership, and problem-solving abilities.\r\nThe proposed interventions are scalable, measurable, and capable of creating long-term social impact. Your CSR support will directly contribute to empowering students from diverse socio-economic backgrounds and help them become confident, skilled, employable, and socially responsible citizens.\r\nWe sincerely invite your esteemed organization to partner with us in this mission. Your financial support will enable us to extend the reach of Project UDDAN to thousands of deserving beneficiaries who otherwise may not have access to such transformative opportunities.\r\nWe would be grateful for an opportunity to present the project in detail and discuss how this initiative can be aligned with your CSR objectives and ESG commitments. Together, we can create a meaningful and sustainable impact in the lives of young Indians and contribute towards nation-building.\r\nWe look forward to your positive consideration and partnership.\r\nThank you for your valuable time and support.\r\nTogether We Can & We Will Make a Difference……………………..\r\n\r\nWith Thanks & Regards,\r\n\r\nRashmi Ranjan\r\nFounder & CEO-(Projects) “UDDAN” (U.P & Delhi Govt.RecommendedChange Management For All)|| UTTHAN(Women Empowerment&Skill Development) || PEHCHAN(Environmental Protection & Cattle Management)\r\nAn initiative by Surya Veena Adarsh Niketan Trust\r\nSr.Business Associate(Honarary):-Indian Ex-Defence Service Employees Chamber of Commerce and Industry, ( IESECCI )\r\nMedia Incharge :- Gorakhpur Udyog Vyapar Mandal\r\nContact No.:- +91-7233977770/7034777277(Both Calling +Whatsapp)\r\nE-Mail Id :- rashmiranjan@svantindia.org,in \r\nUDDAN YouTube Channel  : https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCUW4673Mmtb_IRIlr7S5UFg/videos?disable_polymer=1\r\nLinkedin URL :- www.linkedin.com/in/rashmi-ranjan-b796169   \r\nWebsite :- www.svantindia.org.in \r\n(CSR-1 & 12AA& AB & 80G Certified & Regd. On Darpan Portal(Niti Aayog-Govt.of India)\r\n\r\n', '2026-06-12 05:39:32'),
